            <div class="commercial-step-num">2</div>
            <h4 class="commercial-step-title">Receive Signed License Key</h4>
            <p class="commercial-step-desc">Your confirmation contains an Ed25519 offline entitlement token (e.g. <code>DCL-PRO-ACME-8821B47C9</code>) encoding your node quota, support SLA, and customer organization.</p>
          </div>

          <!-- Step 3 -->
          <div class="commercial-step-card">
            <div class="commercial-step-num">3</div>
            <h4 class="commercial-step-title">One-Line CLI Activation</h4>
            <p class="commercial-step-desc">Run <code>dcouplr auth login</code> in your terminal or configure <code>DCOUPLR_LICENSE_KEY</code>. The CLI validates the key offline inside your volatile RAM boundary with $0 egress.</p>
            <div class="download-snippet-box" style="margin-top: 0.75rem; background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.6);">
              <span class="download-snippet-text">curl -fsSL https://dcouplr.com/install-enterprise.sh | sh</span>
              <button type="button" class="btn-copy-snippet" data-copy="curl -fsSL https://dcouplr.com/install-enterprise.sh | sh" aria-label="Copy Enterprise Linux/macOS curl command">Copy</button>
            </div>
            <div class="download-snippet-box" style="margin-top: 0.35rem; background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.6);">
              <span class="download-snippet-text">irm https://dcouplr.com/install-enterprise.ps1 | iex</span>
              <button type="button" class="btn-copy-snippet" data-copy="irm https://dcouplr.com/install-enterprise.ps1 | iex" aria-label="Copy Enterprise PowerShell command">Copy</button>
            </div>
